  "theorem": {
    "actual_subalgebra_scope": "The bound applies to a reusable characteristic-zero multiplication-closed representation containing the actual deck element U. It permits nonlinear convolution products and arbitrary powers inside that representation.",
    "ambient_algebra": "A=Q[C_q]=Q[X]/(X^q-1), for prime q, with cyclic convolution as multiplication.",
    "ambient_crt_decomposition": "A is isomorphic to Q direct-product Q(zeta_q), because X^q-1=(X-1)Phi_q and Phi_q is irreducible over Q.",
    "ambient_quotient_rigidity": "The only unital rational algebra quotient dimensions are 1, q-1, and q. The one-dimensional quotient is augmentation and discards every nonconstant cyclic component.",
    "atom_marginal_scope": "The same representation must carry U^5 and its cyclic shifts to emit d_a(y)=6[U^5]_(y-a); no smaller augmentation-only quotient recovers varying selected counts.",
    "cyclotomic_conjugate_identity": "U(zeta_q^k)=U(zeta_q^l) iff kC=lC. The forward direction follows because the reduced binary coefficient difference has degree below q, is divisible by Phi_q, and has coefficient sum zero, so it is the zero polynomial.",
    "cyclotomic_degree": "[Q(U(zeta_q)):Q]=(q-1)/|H_C|.",
    "deck_element": "U=sum_(a in C) X^a for a proper nonempty binary deck C.",
    "excluded_models": "This is not a time lower bound for a bounded-depth circuit specialized only to U^6 and the fixed marker batch. It does not cover adaptive RAM or cell-probe structures, bounded error, nonhomomorphic encodings, or implicit summation-polynomial/FFE elimination.",
    "multiplier_stabilizer": "H_C={k in F_q^*: kC=C}.",
    "novelty_status": "elementary_derivation_novelty_unverified",
    "stabilizer_size_bound": "If C contains a nonzero atom, every nonzero H_C orbit in C has size |H_C|. Hence |H_C|<=|C| and the deck-generated convolution subalgebra has dimension at least (q-1)/|C|. The exceptional constant deck C={0} is outside the campaign factor-base families."
  }
